\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Brightest and best of the sons of the morning,
\par Dawn on our darkness, and lend us thine aid;
\par Star of the East, the horizon adorning,
\par Guide when our infant Redeemer is laid.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Cold on His cradle the dew-drops are shining;
\par Low lies His head with the breasts of the stall;
\par Angels adore Him in slumber reclining,
\par Maker, and Monarch, and Saviour of all.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Say, shall we yield Him, in costly devotion,
\par Odours of Edom, and offerings divine,
\par Gems of the mountain and pearls of the ocean,
\par Myrrh from the forest or gold from the mine?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Vainly we offer each ample oblation;
\par Vainly with gifts would His favour secure;
\par Richer by far is the heart's adoration;
\par Dearer to God are the prayers of the poor.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Brightest and best of the sons of the morning,
\par Dawn on our darkness, and lend us thine aid;
\par Star of the East, the horizon adorning,
\par Guide when our infant Redeemer is laid.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

